# Pre-commit hook — LOCAL, fast, best-effort early warning.
#
# This runs the SAME npm scripts as CI (.github/workflows/ci.yml), so what fails
# here would fail there too. It is intentionally a *subset relationship*, not a
# guarantee of parity: CI is still the authority because it runs `npm ci` on a
# CLEAN machine from the lockfile, while this hook uses whatever is already in
# your local node_modules. So a commit can pass here and still fail CI if your
# local deps have drifted from package.json/package-lock.json — that dependency-
# drift check is exactly what only CI's clean install can catch.
#
# Bypass in a pinch with `git commit --no-verify` (that's why the hook is a
# courtesy check and CI is the gate that can't be skipped).
#
# Note: uses `npm` (not `npm.cmd`) — Git for Windows runs hooks under its own
# bash, which resolves `npm` fine; `npm.cmd` was only needed for this repo's
# PowerShell command wrapper.

npm run lint
npm run test
npm run build
